course: dictionary
lesson: 12932
title: Eventually: in the end
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eventually means in the end, after a long time, a lot of waiting or many problems. It tells you that something happened at last, after delays.
explain: «The rain fell all morning, and eventually it stopped at lunchtime.» Eventually shows the rain did not stop straight away. It stopped after a long wait.
explain: Look for clues like a long wait, many tries, or problems before the ending. In stories, eventually moves time forward. In science it can describe slow change: «Eventually the ice melted.»
fact: Eventually means in the end, after a long time or many problems.
fact: «Eventually» often comes before what finally happened: «Eventually, they reached the top of the hill.»
fact: «It will eventually» means it will happen in the end, though perhaps not soon.
fact: Eventually is an adverb: it tells you more about when something happens.
fact: To check, swap in «in the end». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «After many tries, Sam eventually tied his shoelace.» What does eventually mean here? | Never | Very quickly, in seconds | Straight away | *In the end, after a lot of trying
exercise: «The bus was late, so we waited and waited, and eventually it arrived.» Find and copy the word that means in the end. | waited | arrived | *eventually | bus
exercise: Mia says, «It will eventually stop raining.» What does the sentence tell you? | The rain is very loud | The rain stopped a minute ago | The rain will never stop | *The rain will stop in the end, maybe after a while
test: «Eventually, the lost puppy found its way home.» What does eventually mean? | Before it was ever lost | *After a long search, in the end | At once, in a flash | Very loudly
test: Ben tried to climb the wall for an hour. Which word fits the gap? Ben ___ got over the wall. | *Eventually | Never | Sadly | Quickly
exam: «The ice on the pond melted slowly, and eventually the ducks could swim again.» What does eventually show in this sentence? | That it was winter all year | That the ice will never melt | That the ducks swam at once | *That the change came in the end, after slow melting
